(5224, 'apophyge', 'Apophyge', 'apophyge', '<i>n.</i>', '||A*poph\"y*ge', '([uCode:?])', '[Gr.\r <grk>\'apofygh`</grk> escape, in arch. the curve with which the shaft\r escapes into its base or capital, fr. <grk>\'apofey`gein</grk> to flee away;\r <grk>\'apo`</grk> from + <grk>fey`gein</grk> to flee: cf. F.\r <i>apophyge</i>.] <i>(Arch.)</i>', 69, 0),
