(13250, 'bumpkin', 'Bumpkin', 'bumpkin', '<i>n.</i>', 'Bump\"kin', '([uCode:?])', '[The same word as\r <i>bumkin</i>, which Cotgrave defines thus: \"<i>Bumkin</i>, Fr.\r chicambault, the luffe-block, a long and thick piece of wood, whereunto the\r fore-sayle and sprit-sayle are fastened, when a ship goes by the winde.\"\r Hence, a clumsy man', 191, 0),
