(14972, 'carol', 'Carol', 'carol', '<i>n.</i>', 'Car\"ol', '(?)', '[OF. <i>carole</i> a\r kind of dance wherein many dance together, fr. <i>caroler</i> to\r dance; perh. from Celtic; cf. Armor. <i>koroll</i>, n.,\r <i>korolla</i>, <i>korolli</i>, v., Ir. <i>car</i> music, turn,\r circular motion, also L. <i>choraula</i> a fl', 219, 0);
