(20688, 'consternation', 'Consternation', 'consternation', '<i>n.</i>', 'Con`ster*na\"tion', '(?)', '[L.\r <i>consternatio</i>, fr. <i>consternare</i> to overome, perplex,\r an accessory form of <i>consternere</i> to throw down, prostrate;\r <i>con</i> + <i>sternere</i> to spread out, throw down: cf. F.\r <i>consternation</i>. See <u>Stratum</u>.]', 309, 0),
(20689, 'constipate', 'Constipate', 'constipate', '<i>v. t.</i>', 'Con\"sti*pate', '(?)', '[<pos><i>imp. [uCode: p. p.</i></pos> <u>Constipated</u>] <pos><i>p.\r pr. [uCode: vb. n.</i></pos> <u>Constipating</u>.] [L.\r <i>constipatus</i>, p. p. of <i>constipare</i>] <i>con-</i> +\r <i>stipare</i> to crowd together. See <u>Costive</u>.]', 309, 0),
