(25451, 'delicate', 'Delicate', 'delicate', '<i>a.</i>', 'Del\"i*cate', '(?)', '[L. <i>delicatus</i>\r pleasing the senses, voluptuous, soft and tender; akin to\r <i>deliciae</i> delight: cf. F. <i>d[uCode:eacute]licat</i>. See\r <u>Delight</u>.]', 385, 0),
