(26212, 'derrick', 'Derrick', 'derrick', '<i>n.</i>', 'Der\"rick', '(?)', '[Orig., a gallows,\r from a hangman named <i>Derrick</i>. The name is of Dutch origin; D.\r <i>Diederik</i>, <i>Dierryk</i>, prop. meaning, chief of the people;\r cf. AS. <i>pe[uCode:oacute]dric</i>, E. <i>Theodoric</i>, G.\r <i>Dietrich</i>. See <u>Dutch</u>', 396, 0),
