(26950, 'diaphanous', 'Diaphanous', 'diaphanous', '<i>a.</i>', 'Di*aph\"a*nous', '(?)', '[Gr. [uCode:?], fr. [uCode:?]\r to show or shine through; <grk>dia`</grk> through + [uCode:?] to show, and\r in the passive, to shine: cf. F. <i>diaphane</i>. See <u>Phantom</u>,\r and cf. <u>Diaphane</u>, <u>Diaphanic</u>.]', 407, 0),
