(26961, 'diaphragm', 'Diaphragm', 'diaphragm', '<i>n.</i>', 'Di\"a*phragm', '(?)', '[L.\r <i>diaphragma</i>, Gr. [uCode:?], fr. [uCode:?] to fence by a partition wall;\r <grk>dia`</grk> through + [uCode:?], [uCode:?], to fence, inclose; prob. akin to\r L. <i>fareire</i> to stuff: cf. F. <i>diaphragme</i>. See\r <u>Farce</u>.]', 407, 0),
