(34846, 'exasperate', 'Exasperate', 'exasperate', '<i>a.</i>', 'Ex*as\"per*ate', '(?)', '[L.\r <i>exasperatus</i>, p. p. of <i>exsasperare</i> to roughen,\r exasperate; <i>ex</i> out (intens.) + <i>asperare</i> to make rough,\r <i>asper</i> rough. See <u>Asperity</u>.]', 519, 0),
