(42946, 'grog', 'Grog', 'grog', '<i>n.</i>', 'Grog', '(?)', '[So named from \"Old\r <i>Grog</i>\" a nickname given to Admiral Vernon, in allusion to his\r wearing a <i>grogram</i> cloak in foul weather. He is said to have\r been the first to dilute the rum of the sailors (about 1745).]', 652, 0),
