(46242, 'homage', 'Homage', 'homage', '<i>n.</i>', 'Hom\"age', '(?)', '[OF. <i>homage</i>,\r <i>homenage</i>, F. <i>hommage</i>, LL. <i>hominaticum</i>,\r <i>homenaticum</i>, from L. <i>homo</i> a man, LL. also, a client,\r servant, vassal; akin to L. <i>humus</i> earth, Gr.[uCode:?] on the ground,\r and E. <i>groom</i> in bride', 700, 0),
