(50909, 'inmost', 'Inmost', 'inmost', '<i>a.</i>', 'In\"most`', '(?)', '[OE. <i>innemest</i>,\r AS. <i>innemest</i>, a double superlative form fr. <i>inne</i>\r within, fr. <i>in</i> in. The modern form is due to confusion with\r <i>most</i>. See <u>In</u>, and cf. <u>Aftermost</u>,\r <u>Foremost</u>, <u>Innermost</u>.]', 765, 0),
