(59704, 'maroon', 'Maroon', 'maroon', '<i>n.</i>', 'Ma*roon\"', '(?)', '[Written also\r <i>marroon</i>.] [F. <i>marron</i>, abbrev. fr. Sp. <i>cimarron</i>\r wild, unruly, from <i>cima</i> the summit of a mountain; hence,\r <i>negro cimarron</i> a runaway negro that lives in the mountains.]', 896, 0),
