(65584, 'nickel', 'Nickel', 'nickel', '<i>n.</i>', 'Nick\"el', '(?)', '[G., fr. Sw.\r <i>nickel</i>, abbrev. from Sw. <i>kopparnickel</i> copper-nickel, a\r name given in derision, as it was thought to be a base ore of copper.\r The origin of the second part of the word is uncertain.  Cf.\r <u>Kupfer-nickel</u>, <u>Copper-nickel', 974, 0),
