(78258, 'prolific', 'Prolific', 'prolific', '<i>a.</i>', 'Pro*lif\"ic', '(?)', '[F.\r <i>prolifique</i>, fr. L. <i>proles</i> offspring (from <i>pro</i>\r for, forward + the root of <i>alere</i> to nourish) + <i>facere</i> to\r make. See <u>Adult</u>, <u>Old</u>, and <u>Fact</u>.]</p>\r \r <p>', 1146, 0),
