(87133, 'scandal', 'Scandal', 'scandal', '<i>n.</i>', 'Scan\"dal', '(?)', '[F. <i>scandale</i>,\r fr. L. <i>scandalum</i>, Gr. [uCode:?], a snare laid for an enemy, a\r stumbling block, offense, scandal: cf. OE. <i>scandle</i>, OF.\r <i>escandle</i>. See <u>Slander</u>.]', 1283, 0),
