(87859, 'scrofula', 'Scrofula', 'scrofula', '<i>n.</i>', 'Scrof\"u*la', '(?)', '[L. <i>scrofulae</i>,\r fr. <i>scrofa</i> a breeding sow, because swine were supposed to be\r subject to such a complaint, or by a fanciful comparison of the\r glandular swellings to little pigs; perhaps akin to Gr. [uCode:?] an old\r sow: cf. F. <i>scrofules', 1293, 0),
