(95830, 'stoic', 'Stoic', 'stoic', '<i>n.</i>', 'Sto\"ic', '(?)', '[L. <i>stoicus</i>, Gr.\r [uCode:?], fr. [uCode:?], adj., literally, of or pertaining to a colonnade, from\r [uCode:?] a roofed colonnade, a porch, especially, a porch in Athens where\r Zeno and his successors taught.]', 1417, 0),
