(101717, 'timbrel', 'Timbrel', 'timbrel', '<i>n.</i>', 'Tim\"brel', '(?)', '[Dim. of OE. <i>timbre</i>,\r OF. <i>timbre</i>; probably fr. L. <i>typmanum</i>, Gr. [uCode:?] a kettledrum,\r but influenced perhaps by Ar. <i>tabl</i> a drum; cf. Per. <i>tambal</i> a\r drum. See <u>Tympanum</u>, and cf. 2d <u>Timbre</u>, <u>Tymbal</u>.]\r', 1509, 0),
