(101742, 'timid', 'Timid', 'timid', '<i>a.</i>', 'Tim\"id', '(?)', '[L. <i>timidus</i>, fr.\r <i>timere</i> to fear; cf. Skr. <i>tam</i> to become breathless, to become\r stupefief: cf. F. <i>timide</i>.]', 1510, 0),
