(101786, 'tinge', 'Tinge', 'tinge', '<i>v. t.</i>', 'Tinge', '(?)', '[<pos><i>imp. [uCode: p.\r p.</i></pos> <u>Tinged</u> (?)] <pos><i>p. pr. [uCode: vb. n.</i></pos>\r <u>Tingeing</u> (?).] [L. <i>tingere</i>, <i>tinctum</i>, to dye, stain,\r wet] akin to Gr. [uCode:?], and perhaps to G. <i>tunken</i> to dip, OHG.\r <i>tunch', 1511, 0),
