(103133, 'travail', 'Travail', 'travail', '<i>n.</i>', 'Trav\"ail', '(?] 48)', '[F. <i>travail</i>; cf.\r Pr. <i>trabalh</i>, <i>trebalh</i>, toil, torment, torture; probably from\r LL. <i>trepalium</i> a place where criminals are tortured, instrument of\r torture. But the French word may be akin to L. <i>trabs</i> a beam, or have\r been', 1532, 0),
