(103154, 'travesty', 'Travesty', 'travesty', '<i>a.</i>', 'Trav\"es*ty', '(?)', '[F. <i>travesti</i>, p. p.\r of <i>travestir</i> to disguise, to travesty, It. <i>travestire</i>, fr. L.\r <i>trans</i> across, over + <i>vestire</i> to dress, clothe. See\r <u>Vest</u>.]', 1532, 0),
