(107794, 'vassal', 'Vassal', 'vassal', '<i>n.</i>', 'Vas\"sal', '(?)', '[F., fr. LL.\r <i>vassallus</i>, <i>vassus</i>; of Celtic origin; cf. W. [uCode: Corn.\r <i>gwas</i> a youth, page, servant, Arm. <i>gwaz</i> a man, a male.  Cf.\r <u>Valet</u>, <u>Varlet</u>, <u>Vavasor</u>.]</p>\r \r <p>', 1596, 0),
